OL,3,GNEWSA'We want your support, do not live
OL,4,Ain the past' say market traders
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhat is a market town without a market?
OL,8,FThat is a question that some people in
OL,9,FPudsey have been mulling.
OL,11,FThe town, which nestles between Leeds
OL,12,Fand Bradford, grew prosperous on the
OL,13,Fwool trade and was reportedly the most
OL,14,Fpolluted place in Britain at points
OL,15,Fduring the industrial revolution.
OL,17,FThe smog may have gone, but a
OL,18,Fconsultation was needed to clear the
OL,19,Fair on what to do with the local
OL,20,Fmarket.
